plan CommandLine
title   Installed command-line host
status  Proposed; pending approval
goal
    Let consumers build behavior, discover and run registered Stories, and query trace artifacts
    through the installed flow-state process. Preserve the production Story executor, canonical
    artifact model, exact grammar, safe publication, and truthful interruption/output boundaries.
    This proposed Plan reports target behavior and no implementation or cutover completion.

outcomes
    O1  Closed grammar and trusted gateway loading
        - The CLI owns command grammar, gateway selection, formatting, filesystem/stream I/O,
        signals, and exit status. It does not own machine semantics, actors, schedulers, stores,
        transition evaluation, Runtime history, artifact schemas, or a competing Story/Runtime
        model.

        - Exactly ten leaves are supported:

        ```text
        flow-state behavior build --output <path> [--overwrite] \
          [--project-root <dir>] --gateway <path> [--format text|json]
        flow-state behavior render <artifact|-> [--section contract|coverage] \
          [--module <id>] [--format text|json]
        flow-state behavior diff <left> <right> [--module <id>] [--format text|json]
        flow-state behavior check <expected|-> [--project-root <dir>] \
          --gateway <path> [--format text|json]

        flow-state story list [--project-root <dir>] --gateway <path> \
          [--machine <id>] [--tag <tag>] [--format text|json]
        flow-state story describe <story-id> [--project-root <dir>] \
          --gateway <path> [--format text|json]
        flow-state story run <story-id> [--project-root <dir>] --gateway <path> \
          [--trace-output <path>] [--overwrite] [--format text|json]

        flow-state trace summarize <artifact|-> [--format text|json]
        flow-state trace proof <artifact|-> --selector <selector> [--format text|json]
        flow-state trace diff <left> <right> [--section <section>] [--format text|json]
        ```

        - behavior check is the only new leaf beyond retained behavior/Story/trace families. It
        builds live behavior in memory through the same canonical diff projection as behavior
        diff. @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O6 owns comparison and completeness meaning.

        - story run uses the same package-private executor as StoryPlan.run(). It adds no second
        evidence model. Trace summary may succeed while incomplete; proof requires complete
        evidence; equality requires both sides complete.

        - The leaf-purpose table is:

        | Leaf | Purpose |
        | --- | --- |
        | behavior build | Compile gateway behavior; atomically publish the required output. |
        | behavior render | Render contract or coverage from an artifact. |
        | behavior diff | Compare two behavior artifacts, optionally by module. |
        | behavior check | Compare live in-memory behavior through behavior diff projection. |
        | story list | Discover external Story IDs without execution. |
        | story describe | Describe a registered Story without execution. |
        | story run | Run the shared executor; optionally publish trace. |
        | trace summarize | Report retained-window evidence, including incompleteness. |
        | trace proof | Evaluate one data selector against complete trace evidence. |
        | trace diff | Compare ordered sections; equality requires complete inputs. |

        - `--project-root` defaults to canonicalized cwd.
        - `--gateway` is required when a command loads gateway code.
        - Gateway resolution stays below project-root; no ancestor search or implicit filename
        exists.
        - `--format` defaults to text.
        - Behavior render section defaults to contract.
        - Trace diff section defaults to the complete ordered section set.
        - Each option occurs once.
        - `--overwrite` applies only to behavior build `--output` or story run `--trace-output`.
        - Unknown options, missing values, repeated/conflicting operands, or overwrite without
        output fail as usage errors.
        - Deleted Story/scenario flags and legacy final/children behavior fail as usage errors.

        - Selectors are exactly `issues`, `timeline`, `actor:<id>`, or `correlation:<id>`.
        - Actor/correlation selectors split at the first colon and preserve the remaining exact
        ID.
        - Empty, missing, repeated, unknown, or executable selectors are usage failures.
        - Selector parsing loads no gateway and evaluates no application.
        - Behavior check/diff produce equal or different, never trace-only incomplete.

        - @plan.StoriesAndModels.O6 owns the inert branded behavior gateway. The CLI loads this
        form:

        - Supporting syntax: [behavior gateway](references/README.md).
        The normative shape is behavior({ app, stories: { externalId: StoryPlan } }).
        @plan.StoriesAndModels.O6 owns non-empty exact app-compatible registration.

        - `project-root` must be an existing canonical directory.
        - Its exact manifest is `canonical-root/package.json`.
        - `gateway` must be an existing regular `.ts` or `.mts` file.
        - Its symlink-resolved path must remain under the root.
        - Gateway loading trusts local TypeScript; it is not a sandbox. Import-policing scans,
        dependency graph walks, computed-import bans, and ancestor node_modules policing are not
        promised. Read-only limits Flow loader/bundler writes, not trusted gateway code.
        - Use normal host or bundler module resolution.
        - Temporary bundles may exist only outside the project.
        - Remove temporary bundles on success, failure, or interruption.
        - Only behavior build/check and Story list/describe/run load gateway code.
        - Artifact-only commands never execute application code.
        - Discovery uses no second shape validator, compiler, or Story registry.
        - It consumes the branded behavior value's supplied compiled app and external-ID record.
        - Accept only the executing CLI's exact flow-state and Effect package instances.
        - Package-identity mismatch rejects before compiled-registry access.
        - Reject structural lookalikes, empty keys, mixed apps, missing app, and empty stories.
        - Reject foreign machines/Stories, second app identity/registry, and path escape.
        - Gateway code can use anything available to the host process.
        - “Read-only” limits Flow loader/bundler writes only.

        - Record keys are external Story IDs.
        - App Stories use the supplied app RuntimeSetup.
        - Machine Stories target only machines admitted by that app.
        - They may run through a package-private focused AppPlan derived from that machine.
        - This does not create a second public app identity.

        - Behavior build/check and Story list/describe acquire no Implementation, Runtime,
        Fixture, actor, sink, or executor.
        - `story.run` uses the same package-private executor as `StoryPlan.run()`.
        - It produces the same checkpoints, `run.end`, failure, stable diagnostics, cleanup truth,
        and private decoded evidence.
        - The CLI adds no second evidence model or public decoded type.
        Trace output carries only the transaction attempt evidence defined by
        @plan.Transactions.O4; it adds no adapter-private remote identity or journal recovery.
        - Successful runs have completed outcome, non-null end, and null failure.
        - Execution, cancellation, cleanup, or trace-write failure becomes `CliError` for
        `story.run`.
        - Partial Story failure stays primary; ordered diagnostics follow as secondary failures.


    O2  Bounded input and atomic artifact publication
        - Behavior and trace inputs use @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O2 and
        @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O4 validation.
        - Artifact-only commands do not load an App, gateway, or boot-domain decoder.
        Standalone fingerprint validation uses only the artifact. Comparison with an actual
        receiving App occurs only where that context already exists, under
        @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O4. The byte importer gains no App argument.
        - `-` means stdin; at most one operand can use stdin.
        - Named operands must be existing regular files; FIFOs/devices are stdin-only.
        - Inputs are stable-key UTF-8 JSON or exactly one gzip member.
        - Reject deleted Scenario/local-proof formats and competing envelopes/codecs.
        - Reject @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O4 share-only artifacts and legacy final/children
        fields.
        - Reject concatenated gzip members, trailing bytes, unsupported compression, and all
        bounds/identity/schema violations.
        - Compression/decompression-bound violations use `DecompressionFailed` or the applicable
        bounded-input diagnostic.
        - The CLI invents no envelope, codec, migration, public field, or diagnostic shape.
        - Never consume, sanitize, summarize, diff, prove, or compress share data.
        - Files are uncompressed canonical JSON with exactly one trailing newline.
        - Stdout contains only the command result.

        - Behavior build requires --output. Story run may use filesystem --trace-output.
        - Destination and parent preflight completes before Runtime or Fixture acquisition.
        - Existing destinations, including symlinks, reject without --overwrite.
        - With overwrite, replace the symlink entry and never its referent.
        - Publish filesystem output in this order:
        1. Drain all accepted sink records before creating the temporary file.
        2. Canonical-encode and bound-check the final artifact.
        3. Create a sibling temporary file with mode 0600.
        4. Write, flush, and close the temporary file.
        5. Commit atomically without truncating in place.
        - Without overwrite, hard-link the temp to an absent destination, then unlink the temp.
        - With overwrite, use same-directory atomic rename.
        - Existing parent directories and POSIX same-filesystem link/rename semantics are assumed.
        - Unsupported atomic publication and destination conflicts reject.
        - Pre-commit failure cannot change an old destination. Failed temp removal is a named
        cleanup diagnostic.
        - A hard-link race leaves the newly created destination untouched.
        - If a signal interrupts one publication attempt before its commit, that attempt preserves
        the old or absent destination. A committed artifact remains; it is never rolled back.

        - After Story cancellation, first-signal handling deliberately starts a separate requested
        partial-trace publication. That attempt follows the same atomic protocol. Successful commit
        creates an absent destination or replaces an allowed overwrite with truthful partial bytes.
        A pre-commit failure of that attempt preserves the prior destination and adds diagnostics.
        The earlier cancellation does not itself forbid this deliberate publication.
        - A run without trace output installs no sink. A traced run installs exactly one
        default-capacity-256 sink.
        - Attempt requested trace output even on execution failure.
        - If execution and trace writing both fail, keep execution primary. Order secondary
        diagnostics as sink drain, encode/bound, write, then cleanup failures.


    O3  One result controls output, signals, and exits
        - Every executed leaf creates one private flow-state/cli-result.v2 result. Text and JSON
        derive from that same result. The exact command discriminant is:

        ```ts
        type CliCommand =
          | "behavior.build"
          | "behavior.render"
          | "behavior.diff"
          | "behavior.check"
          | "story.list"
          | "story.describe"
          | "story.run"
          | "trace.summarize"
          | "trace.proof"
          | "trace.diff";
        ```

        - Help and version output use conventional unversioned text.
        - The private result data shares @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O4. Its undeclared exact
        nested layouts remain @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.V4; no second result schema is
        invented.
        - Export no public FlowCli result or diagnostic hierarchy.
        - Do not recreate Scenario, matcher, or expected-state vocabulary.
        - Do not define a second result, data, outcome, or diagnostic schema.

        - JSON is the canonical machine-readable projection. Text is deterministic within an
        invocation, readable/actionable, newline-terminated, and may evolve prose, whitespace,
        and human-field order. No ANSI appears in JSON or non-interactive text.

        - Success/comparison writes exactly one newline-terminated document to stdout and nothing
        to stderr. Failure writes one document to stderr and nothing to stdout. Each stream is
        constructed as one complete buffer and attempted with one write. EPIPE selects exit 2
        without recursive writes.

        - Typed product failures and contained defects remain product evidence;
        execution/cancellation/cleanup/trace-write failures are CliError.

        - Exit status is exact:

        | Status | Meaning |
        | --- | --- |
        | 0 | Completed, incomplete summarize, or complete equal comparison. |
        | 1 | Different comparison or incomplete trace diff. |
        | 2 | Usage, gateway, artifact, Story, cleanup, I/O, EPIPE, or internal failure. |
        | 130 | First SIGINT after cleanup and partial-trace handling. |
        | 143 | First SIGTERM after cleanup and partial-trace handling. |

        - One process owner maps the result after CLI Effect Runtime and owned resources dispose.
        - Signal handlers never mutate process.exitCode or call process.exit.
        - First SIGINT/SIGTERM follows this order:
        1. Interrupt current work and stop later Story commands.
        2. Retain failure-boundary evidence.
        3. Await non-abortable cleanup.
        4. Deliberately publish the requested partial trace under @O2, after cancellation cleanup.
        5. Emit a signal-specific interruption CliError.
        - The deliberate partial trace retains accepted evidence, failure boundary, and cleanup
        truth; it never fabricates run.end. Its successful commit may change the destination after
        cancellation. A failed write preserves execution/cancellation as primary.

        - Cleanup and trace-write failures are ordered secondary diagnostics. They do not alter
        exit 130 or 143. Decide commit success from the atomic operation, never signal timing.
        - A second signal may terminate immediately. SIGKILL and host loss have no cleanup
        guarantee.
        - Do not promise post-commit rollback. Finalize discovery/artifact temp files before
        return.

        - Comparison/query meaning belongs to @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O6; the following
        process projections preserve that owner's complete/incomplete distinctions.
        - trace summarize reports counts and timeline as retained-window evidence. Include
        truncatedBeforeSequence. An incomplete summary exits 0.
        - trace proof requires complete evidence and emits EvidenceUnavailable with the truncation
        marker otherwise. Never claim proof from incomplete evidence.
        - trace diff is equal only when both inputs are complete and every selected section
        matches.
        - Differing retained facts are different, even when truncated.
        - Matching retained facts with truncation are incomplete.
        - Selectable sections are event-sequence, transitions, state-changes, issues,
        resource-patches, resource-freshness, transaction-outcomes, stream-outcomes, and
        timer-behavior.
        - An absent actor/correlation in truncated data is not ordinary unknown.
        - Complete-artifact absence has the UnknownSelector meaning. The canonical diagnostic
        mapping follows @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O6: Failure/InvalidArtifactOperand, with the
        exact reason/path/marker/selector. The CLI preserves that diagnostic at stderr and exits 2;
        it emits nothing to stdout. No code or expected-error family is added.
        - Incompatible app/AppPlan identity is an exit-2 failure, not an ordinary difference.


    O4  Fresh installed binary matches source and packed consumers
        - The source handler, parser, and codec tests use the same vectors as a fresh packed
        binary.
        - Build first, then run the installed consumer shim from a read-only project.
        - Checked-in or previously generated dist never satisfies acceptance.
        - Proof checks exact grammar, rejected legacy flags, gateway containment, and loader
        inertness.
        - Proof checks temp cleanup, undeclared imports, and package identity.
        - Proof checks text/JSON parity, stdout/stderr, every exit status, and stdin.
        - Proof checks all @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O2 bounds, hostile identity, and atomic
        replacement.
        - Proof checks direct/CLI Story parity, zero-history and one-sink runs, and partial
        traces.
        - Proof checks exact actor-evidence lookup, run.end, and module-tooling ownership.
        - Proof checks compound states, context requirements, lifecycle records, and operation
        IDs.
        - Proof checks real signals and complete, different, and truncated comparisons.
        - Proof checks deleted declaration/export surfaces and current consumers/root gates.
        - @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O4 owns exact envelope, version, nested fields, Cause, and
        diagnostics.
decisions
    D1  The CLI delegates app semantics and artifact schemas to their production owners
        - Gateway loading selects one supplied branded app; the production Runtime/Story executor
        and the package-private decoded artifact model remain shared with library consumers. The
        CLI owns parsing/projection/process behavior, not a second implementation of Flow
        meaning.

        - Artifact validation is delegated to @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O2 and
        @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O4.
    D2  Artifact-only commands stay inert and publication is atomic
        - Behavior/trace artifact commands operate on bounded validated bytes without loading
        application code. Runtime/Fixture acquisition follows destination preflight. Publication
        uses a same-directory temporary and one atomic commit boundary; first-signal behavior
        follows that boundary.
    D3  Story execution has one executor and one evidence model
        - story.run uses the same package-private executor as StoryPlan.run; discovery commands do
        not acquire Implementation, Runtime, fixture, actor, sink, or executor. The shared
        decoder model is private and is not exposed as a public package type.
constraints
    C1  Keep process hosting separate from runtime, schema, and Story semantics
        - No CLI-owned machine rules, actors, schedulers, stores, runtime history, Story model,
        decoder, public FlowCli hierarchy, competing codec, or share-artifact consumption.
        @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O2 and @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O4 owns structural
        validation and schemas.
    C2  Keep grammar, selection, and path containment exact
        - Add no extra leaves, flags, or selector forms.
        - Add no implicit gateway resolution or ancestor lookup.
        - Do not execute selectors or permit path escape.
        - Reject structural gateway lookalikes and a second app identity.
        - Never claim gateway code is sandboxed.
    C3  Keep result publication and interruption boundaries exact
        - Do not permit partial stream writes, stdout/stderr mixing, or in-place truncation.
        - Preserve the destination until commit; always run required cleanup.
        - Keep exit status exact and never recurse after EPIPE.
        - Do not infer signal handling from wall-clock time.
        - Do not guarantee cleanup after SIGKILL or host loss.
    C4  No evidence or route restoration is implied
        Every Verification entry below is PLANNED. No proposed contract source, process, build, or 
        packed
        proof has run. @plan.PackageContract.O1 owns package routes and restoration gates.
verification
    V1  Grammar, gateway, and inert-discovery proof
        - Outcome: @O1.
        - Scenario:
        - Test each accepted command, option, default, and rejected legacy form.
        - Test selector parsing with first-colon IDs and executable inputs.
        - Test root, manifest, symlink, path, package identity, and branded gateway boundaries.
        - Test app/machine Story registration and all artifact-only commands.
        - Use a gateway that would fail if an artifact-only command loaded it.
        - Pass:
        - Only ten leaves and exact selectors parse.
        - Gateway loading stays under canonical root and rejects identity before registry access.
        - The loader removes temporary output and runs only on allowed leaves.
        - Artifact-only commands execute no app code.
        - Discovery constructs no Runtime, Story, actor, sink, or executor.
        - Check: `nub run --filter flow-state-rewrite check:types` and `nub run test`.
        - Target: add parser/gateway tests under `packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/cli/tests`.
        - Status: PLANNED; no proposed contract parser/gateway proof has run.

    V2  Input bounds and atomic publication proof
        - Outcome: @O2.
        - Scenario:
        - Feed stdin/files, gzip/JSON, malformed values, and oversized inputs.
        - Race output creation; test symlinks, temp permissions, and failed flush/close/commit.
        - Test signals before/after commit, sink draining, and partial traces on execution
        failure.
        - Pass:
        - The shared codec decides input validity; destination preflight precedes Runtime
        acquisition.
        - Commits are atomic; pre-commit errors preserve old or absent output.
        - Post-commit output remains; sink count and diagnostic order match the contract.

        - Combined signal scenario: send first SIGINT/SIGTERM during a Story with valid requested
        trace output. Test both absent and overwrite destinations. Successful deliberate partial
        publication commits truthful partial bytes after cleanup and still exits 130/143.
        - Gate an interrupted publication before its commit; that attempt preserves the old or
        absent destination. Separately fail the deliberate partial write before commit; it also
        preserves its prior destination and adds ordered secondary diagnostics.
        - Observe actual commit results, accepted-prefix/cleanup evidence, and filesystem bytes.
        Do not infer a commit winner from elapsed time or signal arrival alone.
        - Check: `nub run --filter flow-state-rewrite check:types` and `nub run test`.
        - Target: add input/publication tests under `packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/cli/tests`.
        - Status: PLANNED; no proposed contract input/publication proof has run.

    V3  Result, trace projection, process exit, and signal proof
        - Outcome: @O3.
        - Scenario:
        - Verify canonical JSON/text parity, output streams, EPIPE, and every exit mapping.
        - Compare complete, different, and incomplete traces; test absent selectors under
        truncation.
        - Send first and second SIGINT/SIGTERM around cleanup and publication.
        - Pass:
        - One private result drives both formats; each stream uses one complete buffer and write.
        - Stdout and stderr stay exclusive; trace proof never claims incomplete evidence.
        - Status and diagnostics preserve exact cleanup and signal precedence. First-signal tests
        combine running Story cancellation, cleanup, deliberate partial publication, output streams,
        and exit 130/143. A second signal retains its immediate-termination allowance.
        - Drive both named query failures through
        the installed CLI and decode their diagnostics with the production Diagnostic schema.
        Assert Failure/InvalidArtifactOperand, the exact reason/path/marker/selector,
        stderr-only output, empty stdout, and exit 2.
        - Check: `nub run --filter flow-state-rewrite check:types` and `nub run test`.
        - Target: add process-result tests under `packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/cli/tests`.
        - Status: PLANNED; no proposed contract result/process proof has run.

    V4  Fresh binary and packed consumer proof
        - Outcome: @O4.
        - Scenario:
        - Build a fresh package and run the installed consumer shim from a read-only project.
        - Use the same positive and negative vectors as source tests.
        - Pass:
        - Fresh packaged behavior matches all source vectors; stale dist cannot satisfy
        acceptance.
        - Deleted exports remain absent and current consumers pass the root gate.
        - Check: `nub run --filter flow-state-rewrite build` and `nub run --filter
        flow-state-rewrite check:packed-consumers`.
        - Status: PLANNED; no fresh source/binary parity proof has run.
